cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  BSARD Evaluation (RQ3): A Reusable Multi-Tier Retrieval
  and Autonomous Evaluation Harness for Belgian Statutory Law
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using these
  metadata. Please also cite the underlying BSARD dataset
  (see DATA_LICENSE.md).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Marios
    family-names: Paschalidis
    email: paschalidismarios@gmail.com
    affiliation: KU Leuven
repository-code: "https://github.com/MariusPasch/bsard-rag-thesis"
abstract: >-
  A reusable evaluation harness for retrieval-augmented
  generation over the Belgian Statutory Article Retrieval
  Dataset (BSARD). It implements a four-tier metric stack —
  efficiency, BSARD paper replication, full supervised IR
  metrics, and autonomous (reference-free) LLM-based metrics
  (UMBRELA, eRAG, ARES, RAGAS) — and underpins the RQ3
  investigation of whether autonomous metrics can replace
  supervised retrieval evaluation, conducted as part of a
  master's thesis at KU Leuven.
keywords:
  - information retrieval
  - legal NLP
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - autonomous evaluation
  - LLM-as-a-judge
  - BSARD
